    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0168" n="118" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg118"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1616</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Moscow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Summers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-16T13:00:00+02:31"><hi rendition="#italic">April 16, 1918,
                                1 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 18, 7 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>359. Your March 27, 7 p.m., and previous telegrams relating shoes. Runov states
                    Fabian already contracted for 1,000,000 pair shoes with Endicott [Johnson,
                    through?] Sherman, and will possibly order 4,000,000 more at price between 45
                    and 50 rubles delivered Moscow. … Moscow Supply Committee supported by
                    cooperative subordinates in surrounding governments which place orders through
                    it. They say they can get shoes mentioned in your March 27, 7 p.m., to members
                    Cooperative Society and will give guaranties that same will not fall into
                    enemy’s hands. In case shipment is made I have to suggest that removal from port
                    be conditioned on future developments as situation very uncertain, also suggest
                    that Consulate General shall be consulted before distribution made.</p>
                <p>The situation in Siberia and in central Russia should be watched carefully before
                    landing cargo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summers</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
